packages/rekordbox-library/src/pssi.ts.content:
`isLabelTable` validates only a subset of the required fields: `moods`, `unknownTemplate` and `unknownSection` are never checked (nor is the shape of any `highVariants` entry). A table missing these passes the guard, defeating the fail-fast intent, and then fails later in ways that are hard to trace:
- `phraseLabel` does `t.moods[String(mood)]` -> `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined`;
- `labelOrUnknown` runs `table().unknownTemplate.replace(...)` -> `undefined.replace` TypeError;
- `normalizeSection` returns `t.unknownSection` typed as `string` but actually `undefined` (silent wrong value).
Add explicit checks for these fields (and reject arrays, since `typeof [] === "object"`).
